[0;33mThe figure shows a short Stage 1 hotspot migration path concentrated near longitude about -117.53 to -117.48 and latitude about 35.66 to 35.73. The colored, connected points form a compact track rather than a broad cloud, indicating a localized migration path.

Directionality:
- The path appears to begin near the higher-latitude western point around ~35.73, -117.53.
- It then shifts southward, and subsequently bends eastward to slightly northeastward toward ~35.69–35.70, -117.49.
- Overall, the trajectory is curved/hook-shaped rather than a straight-line migration.

Relation to the Mw 6.4 and Mw 7.1 epicenters:
- The red star, interpreted as the Mw 6.4 epicenter, lies west-northwest of the hotspot cluster, clearly separated from the path.
- The cyan star, interpreted as the Mw 7.1 epicenter, lies immediately to the northeast/east of the later part of the path and is much closer to the hotspot sequence than the red star.

Interpretation:
